    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d549-a1">

                <pb facs="0790" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg776"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex 1]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreword to</hi> PPS/28/2, <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 26, 1948 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Infra</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p>This document consists of three sections:</p>
                <p>The first section contains the Department of State’s recommendations with respect
                    to United States policy toward Japan.</p>
                <p>The second section consists of memoranda of conversations held by Mr. George F.
                    Kennan, Director of the Policy Planning Staff of the Department of State, with
                    General MacArthur during Mr. Kennan’s recent trip to Japan.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d549-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The third section consists of the observations of Mr. Kennan based on his trip to
                        Japan.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d549-f2"/> These observations should not be
                    regarded as an expression of the official views of the Department of State.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
